    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4984" root="جبل" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَبْلَةٌ</span></b>  (K, TA, [in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَبَلَةٌ</span>,]) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِبْلَةٌ</span></b> 
The <i>face:</i> or the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَشَرَة</span> [or <i>external skin</i>] <i>thereof:</i>
or the <i>part thereof that is turned towards one.</i>
(K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also, (K,) or the former, (TA,) <i>A vice,
fault, defect,</i> or <i>blemish.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  And <i>Strength.</i>
(K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>Hardness of the earth,</i> or <i>ground.</i>
(Lth, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُبْلَةٌ</span>: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A5-  and see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِبْلَپٌ</span>.

